{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשבת", :translit "lashevet", :gloss "to dwell"} {:he "ב' במסורה הכא", :translit "bet b'masorah haka", :gloss "twice in the Masorah here"} {:he "ואידך אשר נטה לשבת ער", :translit "v'idech asher natah lashevet ar", :gloss "and the other, 'which he stretched out to dwell there'"} {:he "מי שנשא אשה ושהה עמה י' שנים ולא ילדה", :translit "mi she-nasa isha v'shahah immah yud shanim v'lo yaldah", :gloss "one who married a woman and stayed with her 10 years and she did not give birth"} {:he "דהיינו לשבת ער", :translit "d'hainu lashevet ar", :gloss "that is, to dwell there"} {:he "ישא אחרת", :translit "yisa acheret", :gloss "he marries another"} {:he "ואין ישיבת ח\"ל עולה מן המנין", :translit "v'ein yeshivat ch\"l olah min ha-minyan", :gloss "and a dwelling of [outside the land] does not count toward the tally"} {:he "דכתיב לשבת אברם בארץ כנען", :translit "d'katuv lashevet avram b'eretz k'na'an", :gloss "as written, 'Abram's dwelling in the land of Canaan'"} {:he "פירוש כשישב ער בארץ כנען", :translit "pirush k'she-yashav ar b'eretz k'na'an", :gloss "meaning, when he dwelt there in the land of Canaan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לשבת" "אשר נטה לשבת ער"]} {:kind :other, :note "Halakhic principle from Mishnah Yevamot 6:6: ten years without child obligates taking a second wife; years outside the Land of Israel do not count toward the ten."}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Yevamot 6:6 states that if a man married a woman and lived with her ten years without her bearing children, he is no longer permitted to neglect the commandment to be fruitful and multiply and must marry another woman. The phrase לשבת ער in Numbers 9:18 (spelled defectively, missing the letter vav) triggers this halakhic association because ער can be read as a shortened form of עוד, yielding the reading 'to dwell more' — i.e., remaining longer with a barren wife. Ba'al HaTurim then clarifies that time spent dwelling outside the Land of 